1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,817
At this blood-darkened cross, Willard turns prayer into an order.

2
00:00:03,937 --> 00:00:04,712
Pray, God dammit.

3
00:00:05,587 --> 00:00:08,045
-You want your mama to die? -No, sir.

4
00:00:08,167 --> 00:00:09,089
Then pray!

5
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:14,755
Lord, please save my mama!

6
00:00:15,255 --> 00:00:19,089
-Clean the cancer inside of her! -We need your help!

7
00:00:19,209 --> 00:00:22,732
The ritual binds Arvin to a fear he cannot yet understand.

8
00:00:22,852 --> 00:00:24,172
Now you pray, now! You hear me?

9
00:00:24,255 --> 00:00:25,297
Yes, Lord!

10
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:26,880
Save my mama, Lord!

11
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:29,589
Please clean the cancer inside of her!

12
00:00:30,797 --> 00:00:33,589
And don't be crying, you hear? Don't be crying!

13
00:00:33,672 --> 00:00:37,130
-Pray like you mean it! Lord!

14
00:00:37,250 --> 00:00:38,214
Spare my wife!

15
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:41,797
Don't take her from me.

16
00:00:46,375 --> 00:00:51,285
Years earlier, one crucified Marine gave Willard's faith its permanent shape.

17
00:00:55,046 --> 00:00:56,880
Fuck.

18
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:05,854
The sight turns survival itself into something cruel and unbearable.

19
00:01:06,295 --> 00:01:07,961
-Fuck!

20
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:12,836
We gotta do something. The Japs just left him up there.

21
00:01:17,125 --> 00:01:20,995
With the Marine beyond saving, mercy becomes another kind of violence.

22
00:01:28,584 --> 00:01:30,584
Next stop, Meade, Ohio.

23
00:01:32,504 --> 00:01:34,920
Next time, the cops will drag you out.

24
00:01:35,004 --> 00:01:36,587
-Excuse me. -Get out!

25
00:01:36,670 --> 00:01:38,670
I'm just gonna take my break outside.

26
00:01:38,754 --> 00:01:40,379
All right.

27
00:01:41,004 --> 00:01:42,629
-All right!

28
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:49,118
Back home, Willard's silence lets his mother arrange the next chapter.

29
00:01:49,753 --> 00:01:52,170
-Welcome. -<i> Willard.</i>

30
00:01:52,253 --> 00:01:55,045
Willard, I've asked Helen to sit with us. Go on, Helen.

31
00:01:55,167 --> 00:01:57,380
-Nice to meet you. -Hi, how are you?

32
00:01:59,797 --> 00:02:01,505
Willard just got back, Helen.

33
00:02:01,589 --> 00:02:02,880
-You-- -Welcome home.

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,606
Helen enters before Willard has even settled back into civilian life.

35
00:02:06,726 --> 00:02:07,380
It's been four days.

36
00:02:07,464 --> 00:02:10,297
<i>Willard didn't know</i> <i>that Emma had promised God</i>

37
00:02:10,459 --> 00:02:12,839
<i>that in exchange</i> <i>for bringing him home safe,</i>

38
00:02:12,922 --> 00:02:15,381
<i>she'd make sure he married Helen Hatton.</i>

39
00:02:16,047 --> 00:02:19,089
<i>The girl's family burned up</i> <i>in a house fire</i>

40
00:02:19,209 --> 00:02:23,539
Emma sees two wounded young people and mistakes proximity for providence.

41
00:02:23,659 --> 00:02:24,381
It's hot, ain't it?

42
00:02:24,464 --> 00:02:26,589
-Amen. -It's bound to get hotter.

43
00:02:26,709 --> 00:02:29,381
Right now, we got two boys from over in Topperville

44
00:02:29,504 --> 00:02:30,713
You understand?

45
00:02:30,796 --> 00:02:31,879
Yes, sir.

46
00:02:39,963 --> 00:02:41,879
Now, you pray on what happened today.

47
00:02:44,462 --> 00:02:46,504
-God!

48
00:02:46,587 --> 00:02:49,337
-Stubbs! -Stubbs, get out here, man!

49
00:02:50,087 --> 00:02:52,046
-Get out of here! -Come on, give me a hand.

50
00:02:52,129 --> 00:02:53,546
Get the fuck out of here!

51
00:03:05,672 --> 00:03:07,380
Now you remember what I told you?

52
00:03:08,084 --> 00:03:11,154
Willard makes Arvin study the wreckage before explaining the lesson.

53
00:03:11,971 --> 00:03:13,221
That's what I meant.

54
00:03:14,263 --> 00:03:16,513
Just gotta pick the right time.

55
00:03:17,422 --> 00:03:18,380
Yes, sir.

56
00:03:19,047 --> 00:03:21,172
There's a lot of no good sons of bitches out there.

57
00:03:22,547 --> 00:03:24,880
-More than a hundred?

58
00:03:26,965 --> 00:03:28,548
Yeah, at least that many.

59
00:03:33,590 --> 00:03:35,548
How about I buy you a candy bar, huh?

60
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:39,881
We gotta get some sugar for Mama too.

61
00:03:40,001 --> 00:03:43,922
One ordinary afternoon ends the moment Charlotte cannot answer her son.

62
00:03:44,042 --> 00:03:44,463
Mama?

63
00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:46,546
Mama?

64
00:03:47,630 --> 00:03:48,588
Mama?

65
00:03:50,505 --> 00:03:53,630
-Mama?

66
00:03:53,713 --> 00:03:54,713
Dad!

67
00:03:55,376 --> 00:03:56,295
-Mama!

68
00:03:57,086 --> 00:03:59,711
No! Charlotte!

69
00:04:00,211 --> 00:04:02,961
Listen to me. Charlotte!

70
00:04:10,961 --> 00:04:14,336
-What are you saying? -The test results aren't good.

71
00:04:15,086 --> 00:04:17,670
The morphine will continue to dampen the pain but...

72
00:04:18,211 --> 00:04:20,336
there's no way we can destroy that cancer.

73
00:04:20,459 --> 00:04:25,136
The diagnosis leaves medicine managing pain while Willard searches beyond it.

74
00:04:26,131 --> 00:04:27,756
Let's talk downstairs.

75
00:04:36,292 --> 00:04:40,002
When the doctors give up, Willard turns to the only power he trusts.

76
00:04:41,129 --> 00:04:44,629
Now... them doctors can't do your mom any good.

77
00:04:53,131 --> 00:04:54,751
Dad, no!

78
00:04:55,631 --> 00:04:59,839
Dad, no!

79
00:04:59,922 --> 00:05:00,881
Dad!

80
00:05:00,964 --> 00:05:04,547
Lord, this here is my boy's dog.

81
00:05:04,667 --> 00:05:08,217
Willard offers what Arvin loves most as payment for Charlotte's life.

82
00:05:14,339 --> 00:05:15,756
Now you take him!

83
00:05:15,839 --> 00:05:17,297
Bring him back!

84
00:05:17,381 --> 00:05:18,797
You save Charlotte!

85
00:05:20,042 --> 00:05:24,937
His promise comforts nobody because Arvin has seen what faith now demands.

86
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:39,629
Before I found the Holy Ghost...

87
00:05:42,504 --> 00:05:45,171
I was scared plumb to death of spiders.

88
00:05:47,171 --> 00:05:49,546
-Ain't that right, Theodore? -Mm-hmm.

89
00:05:49,629 --> 00:05:51,337
-Mm? -Hmm.

90
00:05:51,459 --> 00:05:54,937
Helen reads Roy's spectacle as proof that her loneliness has ended.

91
00:05:55,057 --> 00:05:57,296
<i>Helen did, in fact, meet the man</i> <i>she would marry that afternoon.</i>

92
00:05:57,379 --> 00:05:59,004
Bless me, Reverend.

93
00:05:59,126 --> 00:06:00,256
Bless me.

94
00:06:02,798 --> 00:06:05,548
<i>And Willard's mind was already</i> <i>hundreds of miles away.</i>

95
00:06:19,131 --> 00:06:20,047
Lenora...

96
00:06:25,376 --> 00:06:29,566
Roy stays beside Helen, expecting belief to undo what belief caused.

97
00:06:42,441 --> 00:06:46,092
A waiting camera makes this generous pickup feel carefully staged.

98
00:06:49,714 --> 00:06:50,589
Roy?

99
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:02,321
Sandy keeps calling Roy's name while Carl quietly controls the route.

100
00:07:03,202 --> 00:07:04,035
Roy?

101
00:07:08,536 --> 00:07:09,536
Where about?

102
00:07:10,619 --> 00:07:12,119
C-Coal Creek, West Virginia.

103
00:07:12,202 --> 00:07:13,952
We'll get you close enough, son.

104
00:07:14,661 --> 00:07:16,536
I'm Carl, by the way, this here's Sandy.

105
00:07:16,709 --> 00:07:19,779
Arvin protects Lenora with the exact timing his father taught him.

106
00:07:19,899 --> 00:07:22,422
-Sister fucker. <i>-He would do anything to protect her.</i>

107
00:07:23,547 --> 00:07:25,672
<i>No matter what the weather was,</i>

108
00:07:25,792 --> 00:07:28,464
<i>Lenora would visit her mother's grave</i> <i>after school.</i>

109
00:07:29,422 --> 00:07:31,922
<i>Some days</i> <i>she'd even read the Bible out loud,</i>

110
00:07:32,005 --> 00:07:33,880
<i>and imagine her mother was listening.</i>

111
00:07:34,964 --> 00:07:36,797
<i>Though he wasn't one for praying</i>

112
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:39,880
<i>Arvin would often drive her</i> <i>and keep her company.</i>

113
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:43,488
The birthday gift puts Willard's old weapon back into Arvin's hands.

114
00:07:48,796 --> 00:07:50,754
Happy birthday.

115
00:07:54,879 --> 00:07:55,796
All right.

116
00:07:57,838 --> 00:08:00,421
Make a wish before that candle burns out.

117
00:08:00,999 --> 00:08:04,589
A polished stranger arrives to lead the same church that raised Lenora.

118
00:08:10,422 --> 00:08:11,297
Hello there.

119
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:13,255
Pleased to meet you, Reverend.

120
00:08:13,338 --> 00:08:14,380
Emma Russell.

121
00:08:14,463 --> 00:08:17,005
Nice to meet you too. What you got there?

122
00:08:19,256 --> 00:08:20,506
there's no doubt...

123
00:08:22,089 --> 00:08:25,589
we're all humble people gathered here.

124
00:08:25,672 --> 00:08:27,047
-Amen. -Amen.

125
00:08:27,547 --> 00:08:29,381
Y'all have been awful nice to me

126
00:08:30,006 --> 00:08:32,672
and I thank you from the bottom of my heart for the welcome.

127
00:08:32,756 --> 00:08:34,714
-Yes.

128
00:08:35,297 --> 00:08:36,297
But friends...

129
00:08:38,797 --> 00:08:40,089
the poor soul...

130
00:08:40,209 --> 00:08:44,959
Lenora hears private attention as spiritual guidance, exactly as Preston intends.

131
00:08:45,839 --> 00:08:46,672
Lenora...

132
00:08:49,089 --> 00:08:51,797
have you truly opened yourself to the Lord with...

133
00:08:52,755 --> 00:08:54,630
Preacher Sykes or...

134
00:08:55,714 --> 00:08:56,880
any other preacher?

135
00:09:00,046 --> 00:09:03,671
Come on, she likes lanky old studs like yourself. Come on.

136
00:09:04,209 --> 00:09:08,799
Carl packages control as crude humor, keeping Sandy inside the performance.

137
00:09:08,919 --> 00:09:09,379
What's going on here, mister?

138
00:09:09,462 --> 00:09:11,921
Oh, come on, Jesus Christ, huh?

139
00:09:13,255 --> 00:09:16,172
Pay attention. It's like I said, you're gonna fuck my wife

140
00:09:16,255 --> 00:09:18,547
and I'm gonna take some pictures, that's all.

141
00:09:19,876 --> 00:09:22,909
Bodecker questions his own sister with the patience of a threat.

142
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:27,963
I got another election coming up, Sandy.

143
00:09:29,214 --> 00:09:32,839
Ol' Matthew's out there doing anything he can to try to make me look bad.

144
00:09:35,006 --> 00:09:37,631
Is Carl the one pimping you? That fat son of a bitch?

145
00:09:37,714 --> 00:09:39,799
No, he's working, making deliveries.

146
00:09:39,838 --> 00:09:43,088
for some wrong done to you by another person.

147
00:09:43,171 --> 00:09:44,254
That's true.

148
00:09:45,584 --> 00:09:49,614
Preston uses sacred language to make Lenora distrust her own memory.

149
00:09:49,734 --> 00:09:52,421
remember all the things we did in your car?

150
00:09:56,088 --> 00:09:57,754
I'm saying you must be crazy.

151
00:09:57,838 --> 00:10:01,338
Coming in the Lord's house and talking all this trash.

152
00:10:04,046 --> 00:10:06,046
<i>Look, my advice to you, girl...</i>

153
00:10:06,170 --> 00:10:07,337
Grandma!

154
00:10:08,087 --> 00:10:09,253
Grandma!

155
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:11,295
No, no, no!

156
00:10:14,337 --> 00:10:15,545
Grandma!

157
00:10:20,587 --> 00:10:22,045
Grandma!

158
00:10:24,462 --> 00:10:27,253
<i>No one would know</i> <i>she wasn't a suicide</i>

159
00:10:27,628 --> 00:10:30,962
<i>and that in the end,</i> <i>she was all right with her maker.</i>

160
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:32,503
Oh, Lord.

161
00:10:36,379 --> 00:10:38,421
But you take her into your arms.

162
00:10:39,126 --> 00:10:42,673
Even in mourning, the family asks the same faith for mercy.

163
00:10:46,171 --> 00:10:47,463
Uh, ain't somebody...

164
00:10:48,963 --> 00:10:50,338
saying prayers or...

165
00:11:16,964 --> 00:11:18,006
Excuse me.

166
00:11:22,006 --> 00:11:23,006
Excuse me.

167
00:11:23,042 --> 00:11:27,429
Arvin frames the confrontation around Lenora, refusing to let Preston redirect it.

168
00:11:30,253 --> 00:11:31,212
So...

169
00:11:32,295 --> 00:11:33,378
Mrs. Russell's boy?

170
00:11:36,628 --> 00:11:37,628
All right.

171
00:11:41,570 --> 00:11:43,653
Don't do anything you'll regret, son.

172
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:46,820
Why don't you put the gun down and...

173
00:11:47,737 --> 00:11:49,320
we can talk all about it.

174
00:11:49,501 --> 00:11:53,349
Only after being exposed does Preston start speaking like a peacemaker.

175
00:11:57,089 --> 00:11:58,506
It wasn't my fault.

176
00:12:01,423 --> 00:12:03,131
And Lenora...

177
00:12:04,923 --> 00:12:06,173
was just like this...

178
00:12:07,506 --> 00:12:08,673
this Reaster girl.

179
00:12:10,131 --> 00:12:11,464
She wouldn't let me be.

180
00:12:13,423 --> 00:12:16,548
But I want you to know that I--

181
00:12:17,214 --> 00:12:20,006
I pray for that girl's soul

182
00:12:20,089 --> 00:12:21,756
every night.

183
00:12:24,047 --> 00:12:25,130
Carl?

184
00:12:26,047 --> 00:12:27,047
I see him.

185
00:12:27,209 --> 00:12:31,671
Carl recognizes a lone traveler, while Sandy recognizes the broken rule.

186
00:12:33,047 --> 00:12:35,672
-We don't even know where he's going. -Carl?

187
00:12:35,793 --> 00:12:37,715
-Just-- -God dammit, Carl.

188
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:39,256
He's going to Ohio.

189
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:41,340
No one from home. That's your rule.

190
00:12:44,459 --> 00:12:48,569
Sandy's warning confirms that Arvin falls outside their usual hunting pattern.

191
00:12:51,322 --> 00:12:52,197
Morning.

192
00:12:53,006 --> 00:12:53,964
Where you headed?

193
00:12:54,464 --> 00:12:56,089
Meade, Ohio. You heard of it?

194
00:12:58,714 --> 00:13:00,173
The paper-mill town, right?

195
00:13:00,256 --> 00:13:01,381
Yeah, that's right.

196
00:13:01,501 --> 00:13:05,174
Arvin answers plainly because their practiced friendliness gives him no warning.

197
00:13:05,294 --> 00:13:06,839
We're passing right through it.

198
00:13:09,756 --> 00:13:11,423
What you going to Meade for?

199
00:13:11,964 --> 00:13:14,089
-Just visiting. -Got family there?

200
00:13:16,173 --> 00:13:18,839
No, I used to live there a long time ago.

201
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,422
Damn. That's gonna be one fine sunset.

202
00:13:24,089 --> 00:13:27,464
You have to be patient with me while I get a few shots off.

203
00:13:28,797 --> 00:13:29,880
Hon, give me the key.

204
00:13:30,964 --> 00:13:33,547
Don't you worry none. We've got some hooch in the back and...

205
00:13:34,839 --> 00:13:36,839
Well, Sandy's good company.

206
00:13:45,459 --> 00:13:48,793
A double-homicide call sends Bodecker toward the county road.

207
00:13:53,089 --> 00:13:54,797
I'm sorry, Lee. This is fucked up.

208
00:13:55,297 --> 00:13:56,255
What do you mean?

209
00:13:56,839 --> 00:13:58,255
It's your sister and her husband.

210
00:14:00,626 --> 00:14:04,481
Two measured wounds tell Bodecker this was no random roadside panic.

211
00:14:04,601 --> 00:14:06,030
Carl was shot twice.

212
00:14:06,780 --> 00:14:07,864
Sandy once.

213
00:14:11,548 --> 00:14:13,381
It looks like it was a nine millimeter.

214
00:14:13,464 --> 00:14:15,131
Sandy got one shot off but...

215
00:14:16,173 --> 00:14:17,756
her gun was loaded with blanks.

216
00:14:17,876 --> 00:14:21,367
The blank in Sandy's gun turns Carl's arrangement into a betrayal.

217
00:14:25,423 --> 00:14:27,631
-Jesus Christ. -Lee?

218
00:14:32,006 --> 00:14:34,214
Give me a couple minutes here alone with her.

219
00:14:34,334 --> 00:14:38,155
Arvin returns to Mitchell Flats because every road began on this hill.

220
00:14:38,275 --> 00:14:39,005
Still there?

221
00:14:41,339 --> 00:14:42,630
Well, I'll be damned.

222
00:14:43,797 --> 00:14:45,380
You're that Russell boy, ain't you?

223
00:14:48,922 --> 00:14:52,589
I just thought, seeing as I was this way, I'd stop by and see the old place again.

224
00:14:52,709 --> 00:14:55,581
The burned house leaves Arvin with memory instead of shelter.

225
00:14:55,701 --> 00:14:59,589
Son, I hate to tell you this, but that place burned some years ago.

226
00:14:59,709 --> 00:15:01,339
They think some kids did it.

227
00:15:01,839 --> 00:15:04,755
Wasn't nobody ever living there since you and your folks.

228
00:15:05,297 --> 00:15:08,339
Well, heck, I come all this way, I may as well walk up there anyways.

229
00:15:08,447 --> 00:15:12,197
Sure, just cut across Clarence's pasture.

230
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,530
He won't say nothing.

231
00:15:13,668 --> 00:15:18,108
He keeps walking because the prayer ground matters more than the house.

232
00:15:22,363 --> 00:15:24,988
I never did thank you for the night my dad died.

233
00:15:26,780 --> 00:15:28,113
You were awful kind of me,

234
00:15:28,197 --> 00:15:30,780
and I just want you to know that I ain't never forgot it.

235
00:15:31,505 --> 00:15:35,172
<i>Arvin thought about the days</i> <i>leading up to his mother's death,</i>

236
00:15:35,255 --> 00:15:38,047
<i>how Willard wanted so much</i> <i>for her to live.</i>

237
00:15:38,168 --> 00:15:42,322
For once, Arvin remembers Willard's desperation before judging his violence.

238
00:15:42,442 --> 00:15:45,256
<i>Fuck the blood and stink,</i> <i>the heat and the insects.</i>

239
00:15:45,798 --> 00:15:46,756
Anything.

240
00:15:47,256 --> 00:15:49,215
<i>Arvin said to himself.</i>

241
00:15:51,048 --> 00:15:55,048
<i>And suddenly he realized,</i> <i>standing in his father's church,</i>

242
00:15:55,589 --> 00:15:57,547
<i>that he'd had no other choice,</i>

243
00:15:58,464 --> 00:16:01,797
<i>that Willard had needed to go</i> <i>wherever Charlotte went.</i>

244
00:16:01,959 --> 00:16:05,989
Understanding the motive does not erase what that devotion cost Arvin.

245
00:16:17,626 --> 00:16:21,456
At the ruined altar, anger finally makes room for understanding.

246
00:16:24,668 --> 00:16:28,113
Bodecker's voice turns Arvin's childhood woods into a hunting ground.

247
00:16:29,506 --> 00:16:30,964
Arvin Russell!

248
00:16:32,798 --> 00:16:34,339
I know you're down there somewhere!

249
00:16:35,881 --> 00:16:37,798
It's Sheriff Bodecker, son!

250
00:16:39,548 --> 00:16:41,089
Got some questions to ask you!

251
00:16:41,209 --> 00:16:44,679
The sheriff controls the clearing with noise while Arvin stays hidden.

252
00:16:51,548 --> 00:16:52,839
Sorry about that!

253
00:16:55,089 --> 00:16:56,851
Goddamn bird scared me.

254
00:16:56,876 --> 00:16:59,892
His claim of peaceful intent only sharpens the threat in his hand.

255
00:17:01,323 --> 00:17:02,781
I ain't here to hurt you!

256
00:17:06,198 --> 00:17:08,740
And I know that you don't wanna hurt me!

257
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:12,906
Come on out so we can have us a talk!

258
00:17:13,130 --> 00:17:14,172
I had no choice!

259
00:17:24,630 --> 00:17:27,797
I hate to be the one to tell you this, Sheriff, but your sister...

260
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:30,380
and her husband, they weren't no good neither!

261
00:17:30,464 --> 00:17:33,922
I got a snapshot in my pocket here of her hugging on some dead guy.

262
00:17:34,005 --> 00:17:35,880
You let loose that gun and I'll show it to you!

263
00:17:39,084 --> 00:17:43,470
Every adult calls his choice necessary, while the children inherit its cost.

264
00:17:44,712 --> 00:17:46,712
And that girl that's living with them...

265
00:17:47,548 --> 00:17:49,423
She's just a little younger than you.

266
00:17:49,506 --> 00:17:51,756
Maybe we'll stay for a while.

267
00:17:59,831 --> 00:18:00,914
Arvin.

268
00:18:01,084 --> 00:18:04,467
Arvin's story begins with adults choosing a future on his behalf.

269
00:18:16,876 --> 00:18:20,707
What remains compelling is how Arvin resists becoming his father's copy.

270
00:18:22,737 --> 00:18:24,112
When Dad goes to sleep...

271
00:18:25,381 --> 00:18:28,256
I'm going to bring you down and give you a proper burial.

272
00:18:28,376 --> 00:18:32,851
That weight lands because Tom Holland plays Arvin without easy innocence.

273
00:18:33,547 --> 00:18:35,172
<i>Durham, North Carolina.</i>

274
00:18:35,881 --> 00:18:39,297
<i>Though the poor fucker had been</i> <i>completely worthless as a model,</i>

275
00:18:39,839 --> 00:18:42,131
<i>Carl was insistent on keeping a record</i>

276
00:18:42,339 --> 00:18:45,589
<i>of both his successes and his failures.</i>

277
00:18:45,709 --> 00:18:50,216
Robert Pattinson makes Preston's charm feel practiced long before it turns cruel.

278
00:19:01,418 --> 00:19:05,899
Sebastian Stan and Eliza Scanlen complete a cast built on damaged certainty.
